Flyway migration naming convention: every new migration file must be named `V{n}.{dev}__{descripcion_con_underscores}.sql`, where `{n}` is the highest existing migration number + 1 and `{dev}` is the internal developer id suffix of the author: `.1` = Gabriel, `.2` = Mauro, `.3` = Diego (example: `V131.1__crear_tabla_caja.sql`). The suffix prevents version collisions when two developers take the same number in parallel (`out-of-order=true` lets Flyway apply them anyway). Never modify an already-applied migration.
